      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "# Milestone 1 delivery — Concordia (CAP), Core Design and Scope Definition\n\nHello everyone — the Milestone 1 deliverables are complete and public in the\nproject repository: **https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia** (Apache-2.0,\nbranch `dev`). Below is each deliverable from this issue with its evidence,\nfollowed by what to expect when verifying the prototype.\n\n## Acceptance criteria checklist\n\n### 1. Design document for `cap-core`\n\n| Claim | Evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| The design in one file: the interfaces, the proof they are reusable, the fit with Splice governance, the fixed design decisions with their trade-offs, and what is enforced versus trusted | [`DESIGN.md`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/DESIGN.md) |\n| It addresses the questions raised in the proposal review: the reusability proof point, and what of Splice's governance code CAP would let it reuse (both in §2) | [`DESIGN.md`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/DESIGN.md) |\n| Every term the design uses, defined once; the design and the demos link into it term by term | [`GLOSSARY.md`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/GLOSSARY.md) |\n\n### 2. Documented first-release scope and out-of-scope items\n\n| Claim | Evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| What the first CAP release (through M6) will and will not contain | [`SCOPE.md`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/SCOPE.md) |\n| Every in-scope capability mapped to the milestone that builds it and the artifact that proves it (capability → milestone → proof table) | [`SCOPE.md`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/SCOPE.md) |\n| The bounded governance and auction sets, and the explicit out-of-scope list | [`SCOPE.md`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/SCOPE.md) |\n\n### 3. Documented extension points for governance and auction modules\n\n| Claim | Evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| How the CAP library can be extended after the release | [`POST-RELEASE.md`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/POST-RELEASE.md) |\n| The documented extension points of the domain standards `cap-governance` and `cap-auctions` | [`POST-RELEASE.md`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/POST-RELEASE.md) |\n| Extension points for new domain standards built on `cap-core` | [`POST-RELEASE.md`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/POST-RELEASE.md) |\n\n### 4. Simplified prototype of a typical `cap-core` workflow on a Canton sandbox\n\nThe prototype reproduces Splice's DSO governance **twice**: once in plain Daml\n(`original/`) and once on the cap interfaces (`cap-version/`) — every demo\nruns in both packages with the same parties, action, and step order, so the\ndiff between the two is exactly what the CAP standard adds. Every demo runs on\na Canton sandbox.\n\n| Claim | Evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| What each demo proves| [`examples/BabyDso/DEMOS.md`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/examples/BabyDso/DEMOS.md) |\n| An idiomatic Dso Splice governance reproduction, without cap dependency | [`examples/BabyDso/original/`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/tree/dev/examples/BabyDso/original) |\n| The same mechanisms on the cap interfaces | [`examples/BabyDso/cap-version/`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/tree/dev/examples/BabyDso/cap-version) |\n| Demos 1–3: Splice's three approval mechanisms end to end (`VoteRequest`, `Confirmation`, `AmuletPriceVote`) | [`Demos.daml` (cap)](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/examples/BabyDso/cap-version/Test/daml/Cap/BabyDso/CapVersion/Test/Demos.daml) · [`Demos.daml` (original)](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/examples/BabyDso/original/Test/daml/Cap/BabyDso/Test/Demos.daml) |\n| Demo 0: the container ballot format; Demo 4: a generalization scenario outside Splice's original design scope (two organizations under one authority party) | same files |\n| Run instructions, in-memory and on a Canton sandbox | [`README.md#running-the-demos`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/README.md#running-the-demos) |\n\n## Beyond the M1 documents\n\nThe repo already contains a **first working version of the interfaces the\ndesign document describes**, driving the sandbox prototype end to end. These\nwill be refined through the coming milestones.\n\n| Package | Contents |\n| --- | --- |\n| [`cap-core/`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/tree/dev/cap-core) | Tier-1 domain-agnostic interfaces, the fixed checks, the opt-in toolkit |\n| [`cap-governance/`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/tree/dev/cap-governance) | Tier-2 governance standard |\n| [`cap-auctions/`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/tree/dev/cap-auctions) | Tier-2 auctions standard — work already started, composes with Token Standard V2 |\n\n\n## Milestone verification\n\nHow to run everything — build, the in-memory check, and the sandbox run — is in\n[`README.md#running-the-demos`](https://github.com/unlockitio/concordia/blob/dev/README.md#running-the-demos)\n(Daml SDK 3.4.11 via `dpm`). What green looks like:\n\n| Check | Expected output |\n| --- | --- |\n| Build (`dpm build --all`) | every package compiles; ends with `Created .daml/dist/cap-version-test-0.1.0.dar` |\n| Cap demos, in-memory | Test Summary: **6 scripts `ok`** — `setup` plus `demo_ballot_box`, `demo_voting`, `demo_confirmation`, `demo_median`, `demo_two_organizations` |\n| Baseline demos, in-memory | Test Summary: **5 scripts `ok`** — `setup` plus the same demos minus the cap-only `demo_ballot_box` |\n| Sandbox run | every script reports **`SUCCESS`** — 6 for the cap version, 5 for the baseline |\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\nWe're happy to answer questions here or walk through any part of the design or\nthe demos. We would greatly value your feedback.\n",
